# Upgradeability

Applies when `features.is_upgradeable: true` (see SEC-UPGRADE-001).

- Every initializer: protected against re-initialization AND against
  front-running (who may call it, and what happens between deploy and init?).
  Implementations disable their own initializers in the constructor.
- Storage layout is append-only across upgrades: never reorder, retype, or
  remove variables; respect gaps. Verify layout compatibility before any
  upgrade, and record the verification output as check evidence.
- Upgrade authority is a critical asset: it belongs in the threat model
  (asset + actor + threats), in TRUST-MODEL.md (worst case if compromised),
  and behind the strongest available control (multisig/timelock).
- Tests to demand: re-init reverts, unauthorized init reverts, unauthorized
  upgrade reverts, state survives an upgrade round-trip.
- Record via `security-check SEC-UPGRADE-001 --analysis <initializer-inventory>
  --author agent:<you>` — the automated part alone does not satisfy the check.
